// Houseley-only SLURM submission throttle.
//
// Real Houseley runs have repeatedly and reproducibly lost the first (reads[0]) file of a pair
// at task script-generation time -- confirmed to happen on the launching machine itself, before
// any SLURM node is involved (the literal string 'null' has been found baked into .command.sh),
// and confirmed to never happen under local execution regardless of load. This points at a race
// condition in Nextflow's own grid-submission code, which prepares many tasks concurrently on a
// dedicated thread pool for SLURM submission throughput -- a code path local execution doesn't
// use. We can't patch Nextflow itself, but reducing how many tasks it tries to submit to SLURM
// at once directly targets the condition that triggers it.
//
// Passed via '-c' on every nested dispatch from nf_houseley_run_processing only -- other users
// invoking these pipelines directly are unaffected.

executor {
    queueSize = 8
    submitRateLimit = '10/1min'
}
